{
  "title": "Congenital Dislocation of the Knee",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4046/congenital-dislocation-of-the-knee",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 14 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Congenital Dislocation of the Knee is a congenital knee condition that is primarily seen in patients with myelomingocele, arthrogryposis, or Larsen's syndrome.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with a hyperextended knee at birth.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of reduction with manual manipulation and casting until the age of 3 months. Surgical management is indicated in cases of failure to gain 30° of flexion after 3 months of casting.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Spectrum of disease including",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**positional contractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**rigid dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Structural components include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "quadricep tendon contracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior subluxation of hamstring tendon",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "absent suprapatellar pouch",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "tight collateral ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Often occurs in children with",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "myelomeningocele",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "arthrogryposis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Larsen's syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "developmental dysplasia of the hip",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "50% will have hip dysplasia affect one or both hips",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "clubfoot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "metatarsus adductus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tarek",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "graded by passive range of flexion and radiologic appearance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can guide treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
